<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-the-lane-built`>>

!! What the lane built (the carrier's #/owed rows 1-6)
# Per-seat token ceilings: a watchdog tails the seat's own rollout and stops the seat at 15M (lead step) or 8M (other modes), writing ceiling.md.
# Pool-aware launching: leads refuse above 50% used, build/research above 60%.
# Compaction limits as launcher -c overrides, plus a live-proven canary.
# tools/lane-state.mjs plus &#45;-lead-step: a fresh lead per step over state.json.
# The ratcheted broker: tools/seat-broker.mjs (data-only git plumbing, pinned binary, fixed env, expected old head, race-proof reads), tools/seat-walls.mjs (a bwrap check seat with an HMAC receipt over tree, check names and definitions; a bwrap install seat), tools/tree-export.mjs, and tools/commit-relay.mjs rewired.
# The live-wiki controls: design text only.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/confirm`>>

!! Confirm
(a) The broker never executes lane-controlled bytes with its own authority: hooks, filters, submodules, git config, .npmrc, lifecycle scripts, PATH/HOME/GIT_*/NODE_OPTIONS, symlink/hardlink races. Find any path that still leaks.
(b) A lead can't grant its own push, escape its lane root, launch a lead, or commit outside the worktree.
(c) The watchdog can't kill the wrong process, can't miss its seat's rollout, and doesn't count the wrong session.
(d) The receipt binds what it claims (tree, check names, check definitions) and can't be replayed or forged by the lead.
(e) Without bubblewrap the walls refuse by name and never run lane code unwalled.
(f) Any regression to the launcher's existing modes (read, research, build, lead) and its floors.
Verdict: SHIP or HOLD, findings ranked with file:line, MEASURED or LEAD.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/round-4-your-round-3-hold-and-its-cures`>>

!! Round 4: your round-3 HOLD and its cures
Read your earlier hand-backs first: terra-final/final.md, terra-final-2/final.md and terra-final-3/final.md under ~/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/. Round 3 cures, as the lead reports them (verify against code and tests; trust nothing on its word):
# P1-1: the relay checks broker-iso by realpath before creating anything: outside the lane, every worktree and the whole ~/.lares-scratch/&lt;lane> tree; a symlinked broker-iso refuses with the lane untouched.
# P1-2: the commit message rides inline in the request (cap 16384 bytes; lone surrogates and NUL refuse); the messageFile field refuses as unknown; readRegularNoSymlink is gone.
# P1-3: any watch error stops the seat's own process group and writes ceiling.md, each stop step running even when an earlier one throws; a rejected supervisor SIGKILLs its child.
# P1-4: tokenTail exposes .fresh (a changed total parsed this call); the blind counter resets only on a fresh event; a seat whose token events stop dies at the blind limit (200 ticks).
Confirm each closes its finding with a test that fails without it, and look for anything the cures newly open. Weigh one design cost the lead names: a legitimate run that emits no new token event for 10 minutes now stops. Verdict: SHIP or HOLD.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* Write `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

